    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/6/96036.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, absolutely. But first up front, it's amazing how close things really are and how just a few people can make a significant difference in a very big election. But yeah, there were elections in the three states and some cities as well. But Catholic folks, we were engaged in Virginia and helpful in Pennsylvania, which was we had some really good pro-life victories in both of those states, whether it's the governor's race in Virginia. or a Supreme Court race in Pennsylvania, but pro-life is still a winning issue. And then also what is really interesting and exciting to see is that parents got engaged and said, hey, no, Dan, the day we are the primary educators of our children, E. Myth, Terry McAuliffe, the former governor of Virginia said, no, it's the teacher unions are in control of your children. So, you know, consistent with, you know, Catholic doctrine and social teaching forever, is that now at the end of the day, the families are first and the parents make those decisions. So Catholic vote, we're engaged in on the ground with text and phone calls in both of those states. And it's, you know, our goal is to engage and educate and get more Catholics involved in the political world because that's not only our opportunity, it's our obligation. And at the end of the day, you saw those crazy things happening in Loudoun County, Virginia. in which parents were subjected to all kinds of tyranny by the school board and then the students were subjected to multiple things in their bathrooms as well but the end of the day is the people stood up said enough of it is enough and we want to make sure our schools and our government and our economy were in fact our needs not the needs of the liberal elites",
