    "turn_idx": 67,
    "turn_text": "for our children, we either choose parochial education in terms of Catholics or as many are doing choosing homeschooling. When maybe the Catholic schools might not be available, particularly in rural areas. My wife and I are the parents of four kids. We've done the gamut. We've got homeschooling and private schools and public schools and Catholic schools. At the end of the day, it was our choice. And so I would encourage parents to continue to get involved I will tell you, as a former member of Congress and a former state legislator, it's actually rare where people engaging in writing and calling and catching me at a town hall. But it does make a critical difference. And if you show up at a school board, even if you get shouted down like folks were in Loudoun County, the school board members remember. And they don't like parents to show up. They would rather you ignore them. And so it's not just the votes, but at Catholic, but we want you to show up at the school board meetings as well because it has a huge impact because most folks are, again, as you mentioned too busy, you know, trying to make sure there's food on the table and they're dealing with inflation and the gas prices are going up. Those are the real life issues that distract us oftentimes from getting engaged in the political realm.",
